{"kind":"stack","id":"sep-mix-1","title":"Separating mixtures: filtering, sieving and evaporating","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f4","foreground":"#1d3b2a","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Filtering"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Filtering separates a solid that does not dissolve from a liquid, by pouring the mixture through a filter paper. The solid stays in the paper and the liquid runs through."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which method would separate sand from water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Filtering","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Dissolving","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Magnetising","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Sieving separates particles by their what?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Size","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Colour","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Temperature","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"A pupil has salt water and wants to get the salt back. Which path will she take?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Boil the water away","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Pour it through a sieve","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Boiling makes the water turn to vapour and leave. The salt is left behind in the pan. Well done!"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"A sieve lets the salt water through, and the salt dissolved in it passes too. Try a different method!"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"When you evaporate salt water, what is left in the dish?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"The salt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"The water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"Nothing at all","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Evaporating"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-e","content":"Evaporating separates a dissolved solid from a liquid. Heat turns the liquid into vapour, and the solid is left behind."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which is a gas that can mix with other gases?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Oxygen","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which mixture could you separate by filtering?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Sand and water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Salt and water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Sugar and tea","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done, you finished the separating mixtures quiz!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how filtering, sieving and evaporating can separate mixtures. Keep practising!"}],"actions":[]}}
